   {
    "quote": "Why it matters: the reporting-bias mechanism",
    "url": "https://casrai.org/guides/outcome-switching-and-selective-outcome-reporting",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": ". Publication bias filters which studies get published at all, based on whether the overall result was positive; outcome switching filters which",
    "url": "https://casrai.org/guides/outcome-switching-and-selective-outcome-reporting",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "risk-of-bias assessment",
    "url": "https://casrai.org/guides/outcome-switching-and-selective-outcome-reporting",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": ": RoB 2’s fifth domain covers exactly this — “bias in selection of the reported result.” A registry-versus-publication mismatch you find while extracting data is directly reportable evidence for that domain judgement, not a separate side note.",
    "url": "https://casrai.org/guides/outcome-switching-and-selective-outcome-reporting",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": ": a discrepancy is still worth a letter to the editor or a comment through the journal’s post-publication commenting system; several of the corrections publicly documented in the reporting-bias literature originated exactly this way.",
    "url": "https://casrai.org/guides/outcome-switching-and-selective-outcome-reporting",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": ". Selecting only results from high-impact journals might bias results towards certain journals",
    "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5569019/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "it is probable that industry funded research is more well planned at the time of trial registration. However, for-profit funded research has also been associated with non-publication of trials and publication bias favoring positive results. Hence, the negative association between for-profit RCTs and outcome switching could be due to publication bias rather than superior study quality",
    "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5569019/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   }
  ],
  "突き合わせ・推定": [
   {
    "quote": "State the amendment explicitly in the published paper, per CONSORT item 6b, rather than leaving a reader to discover it by cross-checking the registry independently.",
    "url": "https://casrai.org/guides/outcome-switching-and-selective-outcome-reporting",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
